---

!! Syntax

```
erDiagram
    ENTITY_A {
        type  fieldName  PK
        type  fieldName  FK
        type  fieldName  UK
    }
    ENTITY_A ||--o{ ENTITY_B : "relationship label"
```

''Cardinality notation:''

|!Symbol|!Meaning|
|`\|\|`|Exactly one|
|`o\|`|Zero or one|
|`}\|`|One or more|
|`o{`|Zero or more|

''Relationship line:'' `--` (solid) or `..` (dashed/identifying)

!! Tips

* Every relationship line must include a `": "label"` — a quoted string is required by the parser or the diagram will not render.
* Mark primary keys `PK`, foreign keys `FK`, and unique keys `UK` in the attribute list for auto-annotation.
* Entity names must start with a letter and contain only alphanumerics and underscores — no spaces.
* `erDiagram` does not support `classDef` coloring; use the attribute annotations (`PK`/`FK`/`UK`) and descriptive relationship labels to convey meaning.
* See also: [[Class Diagram]] for object-oriented modeling, [[Requirement Diagram]] for systems engineering constraints.

